00:04:57,500 --> 00:05:03,500
The game has evolved.

2
00:09:55,000 --> 00:10:01,000
Jumanji: Welcome to the Jungle is a adventure, comedy,
fantasy film directed by Jake Kasdan.

3
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:58,500
Four teenagers in detention discover an old video game
console with a game they’ve never heard of.

4
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:56,000
When they decide to play, they are immediately sucked into the
jungle world of Jumanji in the bodies of their avatars.

5
00:24:47,500 --> 00:24:53,500
They’ll have to complete the adventure of their lives filled with fun,
thrills and danger or be stuck in the game forever!

6
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:51,000
Dr. Smolder Bravestone, played by Dwayne Johnson.

7
00:34:42,500 --> 00:34:48,500
Franklin 'Mouse' Finbar, played by Kevin Hart.

8
00:39:40,000 --> 00:39:46,000
Professor Sheldon 'Shelly' Oberon, played by Jack Black.

9
00:44:37,500 --> 00:44:43,500
Ruby Roundhouse, played by Karen Gillan.

10
00:49:35,000 --> 00:49:41,000
Nigel Billingsley, played by Rhys Darby.

11
00:54:32,500 --> 00:54:38,500
Van Pelt, played by Bobby Cannavale.

12
00:59:30,000 --> 00:59:36,000
Jumanji: Welcome to the Jungle is a 2017 American action-adventure comedy film directed by Jake
Kasdan and written by Chris McKenna, Erik Sommers, Scott Rosenberg and Jeff Pinkner.

13
01:04:27,500 --> 01:04:33,500
The film is the third in the Jumanji film series and
a direct sequel to the first film.

14
01:09:25,000 --> 01:09:31,000
It stars Dwayne Johnson, Jack Black, Kevin Hart, Karen Gillan,
Nick Jonas, Rhys Darby and Bobby Cannavale.

15
01:14:22,500 --> 01:14:28,500
The story focuses on a group of teenagers who come across Jumanji, now transformed
into a video game roughly two decades after the original film's events.

16
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:26,000
They find themselves trapped inside the game as a set of adult avatars, seeking to complete a treacherous quest
alongside another player who has been trapped in it since recovering and playing it in 1996.

17
01:24:17,500 --> 01:24:23,500
The film contains notable references to the first film as a
tribute to its lead actor, Robin Williams.

18
01:29:15,000 --> 01:29:21,000
Principal photography began in Honolulu in September
2016 and ended in Atlanta in December.

19
01:34:12,500 --> 01:34:18,500
Jumanji: Welcome to the Jungle premiered at the Grand Rex in Paris on December 5, 2017, and
was released in the United States on December 20 by Sony Pictures Releasing.

20
01:39:10,000 --> 01:39:16,000
The film received mostly positive reviews from critics, and grossed $962
million, becoming the fifth-highest-grossing film of 2017.

21
01:44:07,500 --> 01:44:13,500
A sequel, Jumanji: The Next Level, was released in 2019.

22
01:49:05,000 --> 01:49:11,000
The film explores themes of video game, fighter, sequel, detention, explorer.

23
01:54:02,500 --> 01:54:08,500
The tone is lighthearted.
